  {
    "episode_id": 83031,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83031.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "It has been quite a journey that you have been on. I mean, it's what, 20 months ago, you were on the campaign trail in the primaries vying for the seats as president, and now here you are just a week away. from possibly becoming the vice president of the United States. I mean, there are so many other issues that still need to be dealt with in America, but coronavirus and the dealing with this pandemic, it's the issue. And you see it worldwide. France announcing new shutdowns, Germany as well. In the rest of the world, it feels like people deal with the virus. You know, the nation has an idea of what to do. It's top down. Everyone does it. The people win. They go outside. If it gets bad, the people shut down a little bit, but they're managing it. In America, it feels like it's either the argument is, all locked down or all open, and the Trump campaign is saying, well, we're the campaign of open up the country, and they say the Biden campaign, Biden, Harris, want to lock things down. What is the actual plan for what you want to do when you get into power?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
