        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Public trust in institutions depends on consistent application of accountability across all levels of authority.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The current legal standard of 'reasonableness' for use of force is inherently subjective and easily manipulated.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Reimagining public safety requires investment in structural socioeconomic conditions rather than increased policing.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The existence of a national registry would prevent recidivism of misconduct among police officers across jurisdictions.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Changing laws and policies can lead to measurable improvements in community safety and justice outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.9
