    "turn_text": "My final question to you is... your name. Why does it seem like it becomes harder to pronounce your name the more conservative a person is? Because I've noticed that there are some people you've worked with in the Senate who don't seem to know your name. Is this strange for you or does this like just remind you of growing up? I mean, any immigrant has the story, any child of immigrants has the story. How does this make you feel when you see people fighting about your name?",
